B.F_=new A.aoz("Terms of service","Last updated: October 2026\n\n1. What NO SUS does\nNO SUS keeps your own chat, the notes and files you send yourself, in a NO SUS folder in your Google Drive. You can share files and notes with groups you start or join. You can send a link that opens once: it is encrypted on your phone first and the stored copy is deleted after the first open. You can send a watermarked link that shows the reader\u2019s name on every page, and revoke it. NO SUS shows no ads.\n\n2. Your content\nYou are responsible for what you upload and send. Do not use NO SUS to share things you have no right to share or to harass anyone. Content and accounts that break this can be removed. You can report content in a group from the app.\n\n3. Limits\nA watermark or a screenshot block cannot stop someone photographing a screen. NO SUS is provided as is: we are not responsible for network failures, lost content, or what a recipient does with what you send.\n\n4. Changes\nWhen these terms change, the new text appears here.",0,"terms")
B.F0=new A.aoz("Privacy policy","Last updated: October 2026\n\n1. Data Collection\nWe store your email, display name and avatar in our database (Supabase). Group documents are kept encrypted in our storage and are decrypted on your device when you open them. A PDF you open from another app stays on your phone. Your own chat lives in your Google Drive, which we access only for files NO SUS created.\n\n2. Burn notes and files\nThey are encrypted on your device before upload. For a single note or file, a copy of its key is also kept on our servers for up to 20 minutes, so the recipient can open it with two digits. A 6-digit code you ask for keeps a copy for up to 10 minutes. Then it is deleted. The encrypted content is deleted when it is opened or when it expires.\n\n3. Audit Logs\nTo help trace leaks, we record events such as file openings, link views and blocked screenshot attempts, with the account email and time. Group members can see the activity of their group. These records are deleted with your account.\n\n4. Product Analytics\nWe record a small set of product events \u2014 app opened, first-run setup started/completed, sign-up completed, first document uploaded or viewed, and notification permission outcomes \u2014 against your account so we can see where the app is confusing. These records never contain document names, document contents, group names, or message text.\n\n5. Notifications\nIf you enable push notifications we store a device token so messages can be delivered. Notification text never includes a document name or its contents. Signing out releases that device token.\n\n6. Data Deletion\nYou may delete your account at any time. Account deletion removes your profile, profile picture, memberships, every file you uploaded (including files in groups other people still use) and the group activity records of what you did. Product analytics records and feedback are kept without any link to your account.",1,"privacy")
